    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You have to find the <var>k</var>-th value of a sequence whose <var>n</var> first terms are given.<br>The next terms are defined by these <var>n</var> first terms in a weird way.<br>If you decimate each term every <var>n</var><const>+1</const>-th terms, the sequence built on the remaining terms is the same as the original sequence.<br>More surprising: the decimated terms also yields the original sequence.<br>Beware, the first term&rsquo;s index in the sequence is <const>1</const>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1 :</strong> Two space-separated integers, <var>n</var> and <var>k</var><br><strong>Line 2:</strong> <var>n</var> space-separated integers, representing the <var>n</var> first terms of the sequence</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">The <var>k</var>-th term of the sequence</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0&lt;<var>n</var>&lt;10<br>0&lt;<var>k</var>&lt;10&sup1;⁰<br>0⩽ each of the <var>n</var> first terms of the sequence ⩽100</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">4 1\n1 2 3 4</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n    